{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 10, :comments ["<b>If the iron is blunt.</b> Although the iron is blunt and does not ruin its face, and the meaning is that it is not sharpened. וקלקל is of the doubling pattern, and it is doubled from the meaning of נחשת קלל. Then the strength of the cleaver is exhausted. [n: The phrase והעניו שלא יהיה ממורט is difficult; possibly והעניו should read והענין, and ממורט ('sharpened') may echo ופניו ('its edge') from the verse text; the syntax of the whole sentence is uncertain.]" "<b>And the word יגבר.</b> Like ינצח, and 'I will overpower the house of Judah' (Zechariah 10:6). חיילים יגבר — like strength, as in the sense of 'Elohim HaShem is my strength' and 'men of strength.'" "<b>And the advantage prepares wisdom.</b> And the meaning is that wisdom has advantage over every tool, for it prepares a man and sets him straight without sorrow and exhaustion of strength. וכשר הדבר — a participle, from the light binyan. והכשיר — a verb, from the heavy [causative] binyan."], :book :ecclesiastes, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 10, :notes {0 "The phrase והעניו שלא יהיה ממורט is difficult; possibly והעניו should read והענין ('and the meaning is'), and ממורט relates to sharpening/polishing; the overall syntax is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses [["Wikisource" "https://he.wikisource.org/wiki/%D7%90%D7%91%D7%9F_%D7%A2%D7%96%D7%A8%D7%90_%D7%A2%D7%9C_%D7%A7%D7%94%D7%9C%D7%AA"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:29:02.404863349Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}